WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.680 align:start position:19%
On October 12th, 2026, the Chicago
Police Department made an announcement

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:12.480 align:start position:19%
nobody saw coming. After 65 years, they
finally named a suspect in the murder of

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:16.960 align:start position:19%
8-year-old Gloria Kuvalovich. He was not
a stranger hiding in the shadows. He was

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:22.240 align:start position:19%
one of their own detectives. He had worn
the badge for 28 years, and modern

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:27.119 align:start position:19%
science just ended his secret. This is
the story of a little girl who never

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:32.399 align:start position:19%
came home from church in 1960.
than the man the city trusted to catch

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:38.640 align:start position:19%
killers who may have been one all along.
Tonight, how a single fingerprint, a

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:44.079 align:start position:19%
family tree, and 65 years of patience
finally closed the case. Stay with me

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:49.120 align:start position:19%
because this is not just a story about a
crime. It is a story about what happens

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.360 align:start position:19%
when the person sworn to find the truth
is the one hiding it and about the

00:00:51.440 --> 00:01:00.320 align:start position:19%
science that refused to let it stay
hidden. It was the morning of November

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:07.040 align:start position:19%
12th, 1960 in West Englewood, Chicago.
8-year-old Gloria Kowalix left her home

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:12.320 align:start position:19%
early, walking alone to morning mass at
a church near her house. It was an

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:17.360 align:start position:19%
ordinary routine, the kind of walk a
child had taken a hundred times before

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:23.759 align:start position:19%
in a neighborhood where everybody knew
everybody. Chicago in 1960 was a city of

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.759 align:start position:19%
corner stores and church bells. An
8-year-old walking to mass was as

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:33.680 align:start position:19%
ordinary as the morning paper on the
doorstep. Nobody watched the block.

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:39.920 align:start position:19%
Nobody needed to. Parents did not worry
back then. Children walked. Doors stayed

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:45.840 align:start position:19%
unlocked. But that morning, Gloria never
came home. And by midday, her family

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:50.720 align:start position:19%
knew something was terribly wrong. About
4 hours later, searchers made the

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:55.680 align:start position:19%
discovery every parent fears most.
Gloria was found in a forest preserve

00:01:52.640 --> 00:02:00.880 align:start position:19%
ravine not far from home. She had been
shot. A whole neighborhood went quiet

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:05.840 align:start position:19%
that night. Parents held their children
closer. Doors that used to stay unlocked

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.720 align:start position:19%
were locked for the first time. And
somewhere out there, the person

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:15.840 align:start position:19%
responsible was still walking free. In
1960, a killer could simply go home, go

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:21.280 align:start position:19%
to work, and become someone else in the
eyes of the world. There was no DNA to

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:25.680 align:start position:19%
fear. No database with his name in it.
Time back then was the perfect hiding

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:30.800 align:start position:19%
place. Detectives canvased the
neighborhood. They knocked on doors.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:35.519 align:start position:19%
They chased every tip. But 1960 was a
different world. No cameras on every

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:39.760 align:start position:19%
corner. No DNA databases. Detectives
canvased the neighborhood. They knocked

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:45.760 align:start position:19%
on doors. They chased every tip. But
1960 was a different world. No cameras

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:50.400 align:start position:19%
on every corner. No DNA databases.
Detectives canvased the neighborhood.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:54.560 align:start position:19%
Weeks turned into months. Months turned
into years. The file on Gloria

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:59.360 align:start position:19%
Qualawitch grew thinner, then went
still. The case went cold. One more

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:04.400 align:start position:19%
unsolved folder in a basement full of
them. Cold cases like this one were kept

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:09.599 align:start position:19%
in paper and dust. Evidence bags in
boxes. fingerprints on cards, waiting

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:14.640 align:start position:19%
for a science that did not exist yet.
Nobody threw them away. And that

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:19.120 align:start position:19%
patience decades later would matter more
than anyone imagined. And for the

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:24.800 align:start position:19%
family, the hardest part was not the
waiting, it was the not knowing. The

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:31.040 align:start position:19%
suspect Chicago police named in 2026 was
Thomas Francis McKiny Jr. in 1960. He

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:36.159 align:start position:19%
was 24 years old, a veteran of the
United States Army. He lived not far

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:40.080 align:start position:19%
from Gloria's family. And here is the
detail that changes everything. He had

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:44.640 align:start position:19%
joined the Chicago Police Department in
1959.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:49.680 align:start position:19%
He one year, one year before the murder.
What followed is almost impossible to

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:54.000 align:start position:19%
believe. McCannernney built a 28-year
career inside the Chicago Police

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:58.720 align:start position:19%
Department. He rose to detective in
homicide and violent crimes, the very

00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:03.120 align:start position:19%
unit that hunts killers. Think about
that for a moment. For nearly three

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:09.280 align:start position:19%
decades, he sat across from grieving
families. He promised them justice.

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:13.680 align:start position:19%
Every commendation, every promotion,
every handshake from a grateful family.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:20.320 align:start position:19%
All of it built on a secret he had
carried since he was 24. The hunter and

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:25.199 align:start position:19%
the hunted. Wearing the same star. He
retired from the department in 1987.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:31.199 align:start position:19%
15 years later, he had become an
investigator public defenders office in

00:04:27.199 --> 00:04:38.479 align:start position:19%
Las Vegas and Reno, working until 2004.
That died in 2006 at the age of 70.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:45.600 align:start position:19%
Never charged, never tried, never
exposed while he was alive. So, what

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:51.680 align:start position:19%
finally broke 65 years of silence? A
fingerprint left on the strap of

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:55.840 align:start position:19%
Gloria's communion bag. Decades later,
forensic examiners pulled the old

00:04:53.680 --> 00:05:00.800 align:start position:19%
evidence back into the light and
compared that print to the fingerprints

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:06.800 align:start position:19%
Mckenry had given on his 1959 police job
application. It matched. Let that sink

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:13.199 align:start position:19%
in. The man who had sworn to uphold the
law had left his mark at the scene all

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:17.680 align:start position:19%
along, filed away for decades inside his
own department's records. But a

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:22.720 align:start position:19%
fingerprint alone could not close a
65year-old case beyond doubt.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:27.440 align:start position:19%
So investigators turn to investigative
genetic genealogy, the same science that

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:32.720 align:start position:19%
has been solving cold cases across
America. Here's how it works. Crime

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:37.680 align:start position:19%
scene DNA is uploaded to a family
ancestry database, and genealogologists

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:44.479 align:start position:19%
build a family tree from distant cousin
matches, narrowing it down generation by

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:49.759 align:start position:19%
generation until one name remains. It is
the same method that unmasked the Golden

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:54.960 align:start position:19%
State Killer in 2018. The crime scene
sample becomes a family tree and the

00:05:52.400 --> 00:06:01.520 align:start position:19%
tree becomes a name. No confession
needed, no witness needed, just biology,

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:07.120 align:start position:19%
patience, and math. The FBI assisted.
The tree pointed to one man, Thomas

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:12.479 align:start position:19%
Francis McCannernney Jr. Then ballistics
testing confirmed what the science was

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:17.120 align:start position:19%
saying. 65 years of silence ended by
evidence that never stopped waiting.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:23.039 align:start position:19%
When Chicago police announced the
findings, they did not hide from what it

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:28.319 align:start position:19%
meant. In their own words, McCannernney
should never have warned the CPD star.

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:33.120 align:start position:19%
Read that again. The department itself
admitted that the institution had

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:40.080 align:start position:19%
carried this secret inside its own ranks
for decades. No badge, no rank, no

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:44.880 align:start position:19%
uniform. Nothing puts anyone above the
truth. For a department to say that

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:50.560 align:start position:19%
about its own detective, a man who died
20 years ago who can never answer back

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:56.720 align:start position:19%
tells you how certain the evidence was.
This was not a guess. This was science

00:06:53.199 --> 00:07:02.400 align:start position:19%
speaking clearly. It took 65 years, but
the truth did not blink. For Gloria's

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:08.000 align:start position:19%
family, the news arrived 65 years too
late and right on time. Her brother,

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:13.360 align:start position:19%
Adam Kavalovich, said he hopes this
brings their parents, both long gone, a

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:19.360 align:start position:19%
measure of rest. They waited their whole
lives for an answer they never received.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:23.919 align:start position:19%
Now, at last, the family knows the name.
And the little girl's story finally has

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:30.000 align:start position:19%
its ending. Not the ending anyone
wanted, but an ending. For 65 years,

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:35.440 align:start position:19%
Adam Kavalovich carried a question with
no answer. Now, the question has a name

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:41.280 align:start position:19%
attached to it. It does not bring Gloria
back, but it brings something almost as

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:46.560 align:start position:19%
rare in cold cases. Certainty. Here is
what this case proves, and it is worth

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:52.479 align:start position:19%
remembering. Evidence does not forget.
It does not retire. It does not die. A

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:58.960 align:start position:19%
fingerprint waited 65 years inside a
paper file. A family tree built from a

00:07:55.520 --> 00:08:04.160 align:start position:19%
database that did not even exist in 1960
pointed straight at the truth. One man

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:09.120 align:start position:19%
spent a lifetime hiding behind a badge,
hunting killers by day. But the truth

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:15.280 align:start position:19%
